        ["In the capsular pattern of the tibiofemoral joint, how does the loss of motion typically present?",["Flexion more limited than extension","Extension more limited than flexion","Rotation limited with full flexion","Equal loss of flexion and extension"],"The knee capsular pattern is a larger loss of flexion with a smaller loss of extension. Isolated rotation loss suggests a different problem."],
        ["A patient with a very painful, irritable shoulder is starting joint mobilization. Which approach is MOST appropriate for the first session?",["Grade I-II oscillations in the resting position","Grade IV oscillations at end range in close-packed","A high-velocity thrust in the close-packed position","Sustained grade III stretch at full elevation"],"Small-amplitude grades in the loose-packed position modulate pain without stressing an irritable capsule. End-range and thrust techniques are for less irritable joints."]
