        ["A client doing standing dumbbell curls says the weight feels heaviest partway up. At what elbow position is the external torque from the dumbbell greatest?",["About 90 degrees, forearm horizontal","Full extension, arm hanging straight","Full flexion, hand near the shoulder","Torque is equal at every elbow angle"],"Gravity acts straight down, so the moment arm is longest when the forearm is horizontal. Near full extension or full flexion the weight lies close to a vertical line through the elbow, and torque is small."]
